{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:23195-1","published":"2026-08-19T11:14:59Z","modified":"2026-08-24T18:23:33.972323343Z","related":["CVE-2026-15816"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-15816"],"summary":"Security update for dracut","details":"This update for dracut fixes the following issue:\n\nUpdate to version 059+suse.645.g79fd74d.\n\nSecuritys issue fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-15816: root code execution via unescaped error message written to sourced emergency-hook script in `die()`\n  (bsc#1274432).\n\nOther updates and bugfixes:\n\n- Fix(base): sanitize message written by `die()` to the emergency hook.\n- Feat(base): add escape function implementing `printf %q`.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"dracut","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Micro 6.1","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/dracut&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Micro%206.1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"059+suse.645.g79fd74d-slfo.1.1_1.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"dracut":"059+suse.645.g79fd74d-slfo.1.1_1.1","dracut-fips":"059+suse.645.g79fd74d-slfo.1.1_1.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:23195-1.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://www.suse.com/support/update/announcement/2026/suse-su-202623195-1/"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1274432"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-15816"}]}